  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Wayfinding Line",
    "overview": "**Every screen says exactly where you are on the line.** ExactDocs serves text at an exact library, version and commit, so the UI is set like a wayfinding system:\n\nAround that, the product is a quiet working tool. A cool tinted **frame** (the top band and the window's margin) holds a white **sheet** where the work happens. The text is ink with two greys. One **route hue** (deep teal) marks place, selection and progress. Nothing else is coloured unless it is a state or a library's line.\n\nBuilt from shadcn/ui and these free shadcnblocks.com blocks (no premium code): `application-shell3` (the band, mobile sheet and user menu), `login2` (the auth card), `blogpost2` (the reader's sticky contents column), `changelog1` (the version rail) and `data-table1` (the server-side tables, #434).\n\n",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool tinted frame around a white sheet; the sheet is inset 16px-rounded from `md` up.",
      "Ink plus two greys for all words; one deep-teal route hue; eight line colours only on library bullets.",
      "IBM Plex Sans for everything, IBM Plex Mono for versions, SHAs, paths, IDs, tokens and code.",
      "Flat: depth is tonal (frame, sheet, raised) and by hairline borders, not shadows.",
      "Motion is composite-only (transform and opacity) and explains state."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three Percent Rule",
        "body": "Colour is under about 3% of a screen. A delta or status is coloured only when it means good or bad. Zero is grey.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Route Hue Rule",
        "body": "Teal means place, selection and progress, nothing else. Line colours live only on library bullets. Violet, indigo, gradients and glows are not used anywhere.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Greys Rule",
        "body": "Words are ink or `muted-foreground`. No third grey for text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Literal Is Mono Rule",
        "body": "If a reader could copy it into a terminal or a config (version, SHA, path, ID, token), it is Plex Mono; nothing else is.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Closed Scale Rule",
        "body": "Only the sizes above exist. A new size is added to the tokens and this file first.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-At-Rest Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces never carry a shadow at rest; only floating layers (menu, popover, dialog) do.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** name library, version and commit with `LibraryBullet`, `VersionStation` and `Commit` wherever they appear.",
      "**Do** use only the named tokens, sizes, durations and recipes; add to the tokens first.",
      "**Do** keep one primary button per screen and start every page with `PageHeader`.",
      "**Do** set literal text (versions, SHAs, paths, tokens) in Plex Mono.",
      "**Do** animate transform and opacity only, with `--dur-*` and `--ease-out`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** colour more than about 3% of a screen, or use a delta colour for anything but good or bad.",
      "**Don't** use violet, indigo, gradients or glows; line colours belong on library bullets only.",
      "**Don't** put `frame` behind content, or use navy in dark mode.",
      "**Don't** use raw colours, `text-[13px]`, the default `text-sm`, tracked capitals or ad hoc durations.",
      "**Don't** animate a height, a width or `grid-template-rows`.",
      "**Don't** use a dialog except for confirmations and for showing a secret once."
    ]
  }
}
